"```python\ndef parse_query_string(query_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse a query string using a nested dictionary structure.\n\n    Args:\n        query_string (str): The query string to parse.\n\n    Returns:\n        dict: A dictionary containing the parsed query string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize an empty dictionary to store the parsed query string\n    parsed_dict = {}\n\n    # Check if the query string is not empty\n    if query_string:\n\n        # Split the query string into individual key-value pairs\n        pairs = query_string.split('&')\n\n        # Iterate through each key-value pair\n        for pair in pairs:\n            # Split the pair into a key and a value\n            key_value = pair.split('=')\n\n            # Check if the pair has a key and a value\n            if len(key_value) == 2:\n\n                # Split the key and the value\n                key, value = key_value\n\n                # Check if the key is in the dictionary\n                if key in parsed_dict:\n\n                    # If the key is in the dictionary, append the value to the list\n                    if isinstance(parsed_dict[key], list):\n                        parsed_dict[key].append(value)\n                    else:\n                        parsed_dict[key] = [parsed_dict[key], value]\n\n                else:\n\n                    # If the key is not in the dictionary, add it with the value\n                    parsed_dict[key] = value\n\n    # Return the parsed dictionary\n    return parsed_dict\n\n\n# Example usage:\nquery_string = \"name=John&age=30&city=New+York\"\nparsed_dict = parse_query_string(query_string)\n\nprint(parsed_dict)\n```\n\nIn this code, we define a function `parse_query_string` that takes a query string as input and returns a dictionary containing the parsed key-value pairs. The function splits the query string into individual key-value pairs, then iterates through each pair to parse it. If the key is already in the dictionary, it appends the value to the list; otherwise, it adds the key-value pair to the dictionary. The example usage at the end demonstrates how to use the function to parse a sample query string."
