"```python\nfrom opencensus import connection, metrics\n\n# Create a runtime context with the default configuration\nruntime_context = connection.RuntimeContext(\n    service_name=\"my_service\",\n    service_description=\"My Service\"\n)\n\n# Create a metrics client\nclient = metrics.MetricsClient(runtime_context)\n\n# Create a counter metric\ncounter = client.Counter(\"my_counter\")\n\n# Create a gauge metric\ngauge = client.Gauge(\"my_gauge\")\n\n# Set the initial value of the counter\ncounter.set(0)\n\n# Add a counter event\ncounter.inc(1)\n\n# Get the current value of the counter\ncurrent_value = counter.get()\n\n# Set the initial value of the gauge\ngauge.set(0)\n\n# Add a gauge event\ngauge.step(1)\n\n# Get the current value of the gauge\ncurrent_value = gauge.get()\n\n# Use the counter and gauge metrics\nprint(f\"Counter value: {current_value}\")\nprint(f\"Gauge value: {current_value}\")\n```\n\nThis code creates a runtime context for OpenCensus using the OpenCensus Python SDK. It then creates counter and gauge metrics, sets their initial values, and adds events to them. Finally, it retrieves the current values of the metrics."
"Here's a high-performance, easy-to-learn, fast development, and production-readiness FastAPI application using the specified packages:\n\n```python\n# Import required packages\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Depends, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\nfrom alembic import context\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\n\n# Create a base class for declarative models\nBase = declarative_base()\n\n# Define a database connection engine\nSQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URL = \"sqlite:///database.db\"\nengine = create_engine(SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URL)\n\n# Create a base class for declarative models\nBase.metadata.create_all(engine)\n\n# Define a FastAPI application instance\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# Define a Pydantic model for user input\nclass UserInput(BaseModel):\n    username: str\n    email: str\n\n# Define a Pydantic model for response\nclass Response(BaseModel):\n    message: str\n\n# Define a dependency function to get database connection\ndef get_db():\n    db = engine.connect()\n    yield db\n\n# Define a FastAPI endpoint for user input\n@app.post(\"/users/\", response_model=UserInput)\nasync def create_user(user_input: UserInput, db: db.engine.BaseWriter = Depends(get_db)):\n    # Insert data into the database\n    with db.begin():\n        try:\n            # Insert user into the database\n            db.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO users (username, email) \n                VALUES (:username, :email)\n                ON CONFLICT (username) DO UPDATE SET email = EXISTING(email);\n                \"\"\",\n                {\n                    \"username\": user_input.username,\n                    \"email\": user_input.email,\n                }\n            )\n            db.commit()\n            return user_input\n        except Exception as e:\n            db.rollback()\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=500,\n                detail=str(e),\n                headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n            )\n\n# Define a FastAPI endpoint for retrieving users\n@app.get(\"/users/\")\nasync def read_users(db: db.engine.BaseReader = Depends(get_db)):\n    try:\n        # Retrieve all users from the database\n        with db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users\"):\n            users = db.fetchall()\n            return {\"users\": users}\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=500,\n            detail=str(e),\n            headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n        )\n```\n\nThis code defines a FastAPI application that interacts with a SQLite database. It includes two endpoints: one for creating a new user and another for retrieving all users from the database. The database connection is managed using the Alembic migration tool, which allows for easy version control and database migration."
