"```python\nfrom google.cloud import monitoring_v2 as monitoring_client\n\ndef create_client():\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates a client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n    \n    Returns:\n        monitoring_client.MonitoringClient: A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n    \"\"\"\n    return monitoring_client.MonitoringClient()\n\ndef list_monitoring_data(client):\n    \"\"\"\n    Lists monitoring data.\n    \n    Args:\n        client (monitoring_client.MonitoringClient): A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n    \n    Returns:\n        list: A list of monitoring data.\n    \"\"\"\n    return client.list_monitoring_data()\n\ndef get_monitoring_data(client, monitoring_id):\n    \"\"\"\n    Retrieves monitoring data.\n    \n    Args:\n        client (monitoring_client.MonitoringClient): A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n        monitoring_id (str): The ID of the monitoring data to retrieve.\n    \n    Returns:\n        monitoring_client.Monitoring: The monitoring data.\n    \"\"\"\n    return client.get_monitoring_data(monitoring_id)\n\ndef create_alert(client, monitoring_id, alert_name, alert_level, alert_message):\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates an alert.\n    \n    Args:\n        client (monitoring_client.MonitoringClient): A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n        monitoring_id (str): The ID of the monitoring data to alert on.\n        alert_name (str): The name of the alert.\n        alert_level (str): The level of the alert (e.g., 'WARNING', 'ERROR', 'CRITICAL').\n        alert_message (str): The message to display for the alert.\n    \n    Returns:\n        None\n    \"\"\"\n    client.create_alert(monitoring_id, alert_name, alert_level, alert_message)\n\ndef delete_alert(client, monitoring_id, alert_name):\n    \"\"\"\n    Deletes an alert.\n    \n    Args:\n        client (monitoring_client.MonitoringClient): A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n        monitoring_id (str): The ID of the monitoring data to alert on.\n        alert_name (str): The name of the alert to delete.\n    \n    Returns:\n        None\n    \"\"\"\n    client.delete_alert(monitoring_id, alert_name)\n\ndef create_notification_channel(client, notification_channel_id):\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates a notification channel.\n    \n    Args:\n        client (monitoring_client.MonitoringClient): A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n        notification_channel_id (str): The ID of the notification channel to create.\n    \n    Returns:\n        None\n    \"\"\"\n    client.create_notification_channel(notification_channel_id)\n\ndef delete_notification_channel(client, notification_channel_id):\n    \"\"\"\n    Deletes a notification channel.\n    \n    Args:\n        client (monitoring_client.MonitoringClient): A client object for interacting with the Google Cloud Monitoring API.\n        notification_channel_id (str): The ID of the notification channel to delete.\n    \n    Returns:\n        None\n    \"\"\"\n    client.delete_notification_channel(notification_channel_id)\n```"
"```python\nimport click\n\n@click.group()\ndef cli():\n    \"\"\"A simple CLI tool for managing users\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.option('--name', prompt='Name', help='The name of the user.')\n@click.option('--email', prompt='Email', help='The email of the user.')\ndef create_user(name, email):\n    \"\"\"Create a new user\"\"\"\n    click.echo(f\"Created user: {name} ({email})\")\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.option('--name', prompt='Name', help='The name of the user.')\n@click.option('--email', prompt='Email', help='The email of the user.')\ndef delete_user(name, email):\n    \"\"\"Delete a user\"\"\"\n    click.echo(f\"Deleted user: {name} ({email})\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    cli()\n```\n\nThis code creates a simple CLI tool with two commands: `create_user` and `delete_user`. The `create_user` command takes two optional arguments, `name` and `email`, and creates a new user with the specified name and email. The `delete_user` command also takes two optional arguments, `name` and `email`, and deletes the user with the specified name and email."
"```python\n# Import the necessary Cython bindings\nfrom cython import types, library, array\n\n# Define the function to hash a string using MurmurHash\n@library(\"murmurhash\")\ndef hash_string(string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Hash a given string using MurmurHash.\n\n    Args:\n    string (str): The string to be hashed.\n\n    Returns:\n    int: The hashed value of the input string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define the input and output types\n    input_type = c_char_p\n    output_type = c_int\n\n    # Define the MurmurHash function\n    murmurhash = types.CFunction(\n        # Function signature\n        \"int\",\n        # Input and output types\n        (input_type, output_type),\n        # Function body\n        \"\"\"\n        int hash(string)\n        {\n            const char16_t* string = (const char16_t*) input;\n            int hash = murmurhash(string, strlen(string), 0, NULL);\n            return hash;\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n    )\n\n    # Create a MurmurHash object\n    hash_object = murmurhash()\n\n    # Call the MurmurHash function with the input string\n    result = hash_object(string, len(string), 0, NULL)\n\n    # Return the hashed value\n    return result\n\n# Example usage:\nprint(hash_string(\"Hello, World!\"))\n```"
